# Supabase

- All schema changes via `supabase/migrations/*.sql` — never edit prod in the dashboard
- After migrations: `generate_typescript_types` (MCP) or `supabase gen types typescript --local`
- Apply locally: `supabase db reset` (optional; needs Docker)
- Apply remote: prefer **`supabase db push`** (CLI) so versions match `supabase/migrations/<version>_*.sql` filenames. MCP `apply_migration` stamps its **own** timestamp and **will break CI `db push`** (“Remote migration versions not found in local migrations directory”).
- If CLI dies on `~/.supabase/telemetry.json` EPERM (sandbox): `SUPABASE_DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1 supabase db push` with full permissions. Confirm `supabase/.temp/project-ref` matches **dev** (`SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID`) before push — `link` can leave you on prod.
- If `db push` fails with IPv6 `db.<ref>.supabase.co` timeout or pooler `tenant/user … not found`: apply the committed SQL via MCP `execute_sql` on the correct project ref, then stamp `INSERT INTO supabase_migrations.schema_migrations (version, name) VALUES ('…', '…')` so later `db push` stays aligned. Do **not** use MCP `apply_migration` for SQL that already has a filename (wrong stamp).
- If history already diverged: `list_migrations` on the project, then either (a) `supabase migration repair --status reverted <orphan…>` + `--status applied <local version…>` against the correct project (`--linked` + prod password / `--db-url`), or (b) `execute_sql` to delete orphan versions and `INSERT` the committed filenames (SQL already applied). Then push/apply only missing local versions.
- Never `apply_migration` for SQL that already has a committed filename — use `db push`, or `execute_sql` + `INSERT INTO supabase_migrations.schema_migrations (version, name) VALUES ('…', '…')`.
- **Enum `ADD VALUE` must be its own migration.** Postgres raises `55P04` (“unsafe use of new value … of enum type”) if a later statement in the **same transaction** references the new label. Each migration file runs in one transaction (`supabase start` / CI), so put only `alter type … add value …` in file N, then use the label in file N+1. Do not combine them even on PG 15+. Remote `db push` can hide this when the label was already committed in a prior session.
- Pin Supabase CLI in GitHub Actions (`supabase/setup-cli` `version: 2.x.y`) — `latest` often fails with GitHub API rate limit when resolving the release.
- RLS must enforce auth server-side; client checks are UX only
- **INSERT `WITH CHECK` must pin server-owned columns.** Checking only
  `author_id = auth.uid()` is not enough — PostgREST clients can set any
  insertable column (`vote_count`, `status`, counters, workflow enums).
  Require safe defaults in the policy (e.g. `status = 'new' and vote_count = 0`)
  and/or omit those columns from client inserts and maintain them only via
  triggers / SuperAdmin UPDATE. When reviewing a new table, ask: “Can a
  malicious insert inflate ranking or skip a workflow state?”
- **SuperAdmin UI without RLS/Edge is incomplete.** Site lockdown, super-ban,
  admin lists, and `is_admin_message` inserts must be enforced with
  `is_superadmin()` (and auth Edge `get_site_lockdown` /
  `is_superadmin_phone`). Group soft-delete (`deleted_at`) ≠ SuperAdmin
  deactivate (`deactivated_at`).
- **`auth-verify-otp` lockdown must run on the Twilio-approved phone**
  (`verifiedPhone` from `checkPayload.to`) immediately before
  `issuePhoneSession`. Checking only the request body `phone` misses
  `verification_sid` + code verifies (and any sid/To mismatch). Symptom →
  check: sid-only verify returns a session while `site_settings.lockdown` is
  true for a non–SuperAdmin number.

## Agent-owned Supabase ops (do not defer to user)

Use **Supabase Cursor Plugin** (`plugin-supabase-supabase`) or CLI with `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN`:

- `create_project` — new dev/staging projects (after `get_cost` / `confirm_cost`)
- `apply_migration` — push committed SQL to a project ref
- `get_publishable_keys` / `supabase projects api-keys` — populate `.env.local`
- Auth config — Management API or dashboard only if MCP/API unavailable
- `list_migrations`, `get_advisors`, `execute_sql` — verify and debug

Never ask the user to create a project or paste URL/keys you can fetch. See [`.cursor/rules/mcp-first-ops.mdc`](mcp-first-ops.mdc).

## API keys

- Browser: publishable / anon (`sb_publishable_…` or JWT `anon`)
- Admin / GoTrue Management (`/auth/v1/admin/*`, e2e session seeding): **JWT `service_role`** (`eyJ…`). Opaque `sb_secret_…` keys are rejected by Admin Auth with “Invalid API key”.
- Fetch both: `supabase projects api-keys --project-ref REF -o json` — prefer the entry named `service_role` for admin, not `default`/`sb_secret_*`.

## Membership lists + Realtime

- App group lists are membership-scoped (`useGroups({ userId })` with `group_members!inner`). Keep `group_members` in the `supabase_realtime` publication so join/leave refresh sidebars.
- After `addGroup`, wait until the creator membership row is queryable before navigating — Realtime alone can lag a beat behind the insert trigger.
- `supabase.channel(name)` reuses by name: concurrent `useGroupMembers` / `useGroups` mounts need unique `channelId` (or the hook’s `useId` default). Reusing a subscribed channel and calling `.on()` again throws “cannot add postgres_changes callbacks … after subscribe()”.

## SMS auth (Edge Functions)

- `auth-verify-otp` must treat **new and returning** phone users as sign-in. Look up by digit-normalized phone **or** synthetic email (`{digits}@phone.yowl.us`) before `createUser`.
- GoTrue may store `auth.users.phone` **without** a leading `+`. Exact E.164 `===` match fails on second login and surfaces as “already registered”.
- Session longevity: set `jwt_exp` to `604800` (1 week max) via Management API `PATCH .../config/auth` on **dev and prod**; keep time-box / inactivity at `0`. Local: `supabase/config.toml` `jwt_expiry`.
- **Test OTP (local/dev only):** `AUTH_ALLOW_TEST_OTP=true` + fictional `555-01XX` phones + `AUTH_TEST_OTP_CODE` (default `555555`) short-circuits Twilio in `auth-send-otp` / `auth-verify-otp`. Wire via `supabase/functions/.env` (from `.env.example`) or the **quacker-dev** secret — **never** set on production. **`supabase start` loads `supabase/functions/.env` automatically** — CI copies `.env.example` before start; local e2e needs the same (restart stack if you add `.env` after start). Shared helpers: `_shared/auth-utils.ts` + `_shared/phone-session.ts`. Reserved FTUE number `+12025550199` / `(202) 555-0199` is deleted before each session when test OTP is on so onboarding is always testable; Maestro shared login uses `0100`.
- **Real SMS to any phone:** Twilio account must have an **approved Primary Compliance Profile** (Trust Hub). Upgrade + billing balance alone still returns error **21608** until PCP is approved — Console-only for direct accounts; see [`docs/prerequisites.md`](docs/prerequisites.md#twilio-verify-sms-otp).

## Web Push (notify-new-message)

- Schema: `user_notification_prefs`, `group_members.notify_level`, `messages.is_announcement`
- Unread: `group_members.last_viewed_at` + RPC `unread_message_counts()` (filter by notify_level; compare `messages.author_id`)
- Focused app: SW posts `yowl-push` to clients instead of OS notif; `InAppPushToastListener` toasts other groups
- Trigger `on_message_notify` uses Vault `notify_webhook_url` + `notify_webhook_secret` → Edge Function
- Edge auth: `x-webhook-secret` (deploy with `verify_jwt: false`); VAPID via project secrets
- Setup script: `scripts/setup-notify-webhook.sh` (Management API — CLI may lack `--token` on `secrets set`)
- Browser: `VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` only; never auto-call `Notification.requestPermission`
- E2E push mock (`tests/e2e/fixtures/push.ts`) must stub `serviceWorker.addEventListener` / `removeEventListener` — `InAppPushToastListener` attaches on mount

## Suggestion GitHub Issues (suggestion-github-issue)

- Trigger `on_suggestion_github_issue` uses Vault `suggestion_github_webhook_url` + `suggestion_github_webhook_secret` → Edge Function (same `pg_net` + `x-webhook-secret` pattern as notify)
- Edge secrets: `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_REPO` (default `BrokenLinc/quacker`), `PUBLIC_APP_URL` / `PUBLIC_APP_URL_DEV`, `SUGGESTION_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET`
- **Fail closed on missing webhook secret.** `verify_jwt: false` + optional secret check = anyone can forge issues with the project PAT. Require `SUGGESTION_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET` and 503 if unset (do not mirror notify’s soft skip for privileged side effects). DB trigger must **skip** `http_post` when Vault secret is null/empty — never post `x-webhook-secret: ''` (guaranteed 401 while inserts look healthy).
- **Dev setup must not inherit `yowl.us`.** `scripts/setup-suggestion-github-webhook.sh dev` accepts `PUBLIC_APP_URL_DEV` or an explicit non-prod `PUBLIC_APP_URL` (same preview origin as `VITE_APP_URL` is OK). Reject only unset / `https://yowl.us` — do not require the two vars to differ. Symptom → check: setup exits “Set PUBLIC_APP_URL_DEV” despite a valid preview URL in both vars.
- **Persist minted webhook secrets into blank `.env.local` keys.** `.env.example` ships `SUGGESTION_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=`; setup must replace that line, not skip when the key exists empty (else each rerun rotates Vault/Edge while local curl stays 401).
- **Do not grant SuperAdmin probe RPCs to `anon`.** Export embeds flags via `is_user_superadmin` inside a security-definer RPC; never expose a standalone `user_is_superadmin(uid)` to `anon` (publishable key can enumerate admin accounts). Prefer reusing `is_user_superadmin` (authenticated/service_role only).
- Setup: `scripts/setup-suggestion-github-webhook.sh [dev|prod]`
- Public companion: `suggestion-export` (`GET ?id=`) via RPC `suggestion_export` — no webhook secret; anon `apikey` only
- Deploy both with `verify_jwt: false` (see `deploy.yml`)

## Gitignore (CLI-generated paths)

The Supabase CLI writes local state under `supabase/.temp/` (linked project ref) and `supabase/.branches/` (branch metadata). These must stay **gitignored** — never commit them.

Root `.supabase/` (Docker local stack data) is also gitignored. `supabase/functions/.env` (local Edge Function secrets / test OTP) is gitignored — keep `supabase/functions/.env.example` tracked. When adding Supabase CLI features or other stack tools, extend `.gitignore` in the same PR and verify with `yarn check:requirements`.
